<article class="env-lemma" id="02NL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02NL">Lemma <span data-tag="02NL">29.30.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Y \to Z$ be locally of finite type. If $f$ has relative dimension $\leq d$ and $g$ has relative dimension $\leq e$ then $g \circ f$ has relative dimension $\leq d + e$. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ has relative dimension $d$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$g$ has relative dimension $e$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is flat, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $g \circ f$ has relative dimension $d + e$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/02JS" data-tag="02JS">29.29.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>